190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (This project is based on Pizza Sales Analysis using SQL. The main objective of the project is to analyze pizza sales data and gain meaningful business insights by using different SQL queries. The project helps in understanding customer ordering behavior, sales performance, revenue generation, and product demand.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (In this project, various levels of SQL queries such as Basic, Intermediate, and Advanced queries are used to explore the dataset effectively. The analysis includes finding the total number of orders, total revenue generated, highest-priced pizza, most common pizza size, and top-selling pizza types. It also focuses on category-wise sales analysis, hourly order distribution, average daily orders, and revenue-based performance.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (Advanced analysis techniques are used to calculate the percentage contribution of each pizza type to total revenue, cumulative revenue over time, and the top-performing pizzas in each category. These insights help businesses understand customer preferences, improve decision-making, manage inventory, and increase profitability.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (Overall, this project demonstrates practical knowledge of SQL, data analysis, joins, aggregation functions, window functions, grouping, and business intelligence concepts through a real-world pizza sales dataset.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
